    <briefdescription>
<para>Assumptions are conditions that must be satisfied for a test to proceed. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Assumptions represent essential preconditions that must hold true for a test case to execute meaningfully. If an assumption fails, the test is immediately terminated, as continuing would render the results invalid or misleading.</para>
<para>By clearly specifying assumptions, developers can ensure that tests are only run in appropriate contexts, improving the reliability and accuracy of test outcomes. This mechanism is particularly valuable for guarding against invalid input, incomplete initialisation, or unsupported environments.  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
